From 30d1d3844a568ee974d33d43ff41b601ddff670a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] vulkan/wsi: VK_KHR_display on the PS4's VideoOut

In place of the DRM backend, VK_KHR_display drives VideoOut: one
display, one plane and one 1920x1080 mode. The framebuffers belong to
the process and are imported into each swapchain as host memory, so a
recreated device presents where the previous one did. Presents are
flipped by a thread once their fences signal; FIFO is the only present
mode.

Co-authored-by: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
